mbed TLS patch: guard the PBKDF2 implementation with MBEDTLS_PKCS5_ALT.

mbed TLS 3.6 has no MBEDTLS_PKCS5_ALT module guard in library/pkcs5.c,
so an alternative implementation of mbedtls_pkcs5_pbkdf2_hmac[_ext]
cannot replace the built-in one: both would be compiled and the link
would see duplicate symbols.  Wrap the software PBKDF2 path in the
usual "#if !defined(MBEDTLS_xxx_ALT)" guard, the same convention the
library already uses for MBEDTLS_GCM_ALT or MBEDTLS_ECDSA_SIGN_ALT.
Parsing (mbedtls_pkcs5_pbes2 etc.) stays in the library; only the key
derivation is replaceable.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [NuttX carries this patch so the
cryptodev-backed pkcs5_alt.c can provide the PBKDF2 functions]

--- a/library/pkcs5.c
+++ b/library/pkcs5.c
@@ -265,6 +265,7 @@
 }
 #endif /* MBEDTLS_ASN1_PARSE_C && MBEDTLS_CIPHER_C */
 
+#if !defined(MBEDTLS_PKCS5_ALT)
 static int pkcs5_pbkdf2_hmac(mbedtls_md_context_t *ctx,
                              const unsigned char *password,
                              size_t plen, const unsigned char *salt, size_t slen,
@@ -392,6 +393,7 @@
     mbedtls_md_free(&md_ctx);
     return ret;
 }
+#endif /* !MBEDTLS_PKCS5_ALT */
 
 #if defined(MBEDTLS_SELF_TEST)
 
